= Overfitting — Technical =

== Finite-sample adaptation ==
Overfitting can arise because the learner optimizes:

<pre>
training objective
validation criterion
model-search procedure
feature/preprocessing pipeline
</pre>

against finite noisy samples.

Thus overfitting can occur at multiple levels, not only model-parameter fitting.

== Interpolation ==
An interpolating predictor achieves zero or near-zero training error.

Interpolation is not equivalent to overfitting.

In some overparameterized regimes, interpolation can coexist with low test error and double-descent behavior.

== Selection ==
If many candidate systems are compared on one validation set, the selected maximum can exploit noise in the selection estimate.

That phenomenon is developed separately as [[Model selection bias]].

